1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,559
This is LucentDock: a smart dock for Windows, built and verified in public.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:19,050
Your taskbar shows your apps. It doesn't show what needs you now: the meeting in ten minutes, the battery dying, the limits you set for yourself.

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:36,600
When a meeting reaches ten minutes away, the dock rearranges itself: the calendar comes forward, distractions step aside, and one click puts everything back.

4
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,110
Three styles, including liquid glass, where the dock's material is your own wallpaper, bent at the rim by a lens.

5
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:17,080
Every release passes six hundred eighty two automated tests, builds reproducibly byte for byte, and crosses an attended gate at five display scales before anyone installs it.

6
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:38,180
It is built by Leonel Cortes, coordinating AI systems: one implements, another audits blind, and only Leonel can run the final gate.

7
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:55,730
LucentDock. Download it, verify its hash yourself, and undo anything it ever does. The whole story is in the open.

